ssh3-c (0.5.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 0.5.2: the sftp jail of wave A - the jail
    root is pinned by a descriptor (open O_NOFOLLOW, then the chroot
    through /proc/self/fd), so the user can no longer swap the home
    for a symlink while the child is still root; the privilege drop
    is permanent (the saved set-user id goes too, so the child cannot
    restore the root); and the lexical jail is refused for a
    privileged daemon (the engine's prefix check follows the
    symlinks, so it confines nothing against root).  The password and
    its digest compare in constant time now, the h3 parse layer has
    a fuzz harness (300000 inputs under ASan+UBSan, clean), and the
    release ships the raw linux client and the checksums of the
    assets.

 -- Max <nahual15@gmail.com>  Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:40:00 +0000

ssh3-c (0.5.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 0.5.1: the wildcard listener never told the
    QUIC layer its local address, so the local address path of the
    0.5.0 release stayed inert - the replies of a multi-address host
    carried the routed source address and the client did not
    recognise its own answer.  The field verification (two network
    namespaces: the server with the dialed address and a tunnel
    address, the client behind the tunnel) measured it: the answer
    came from the tunnel address, now it carries the dialed one.  The
    idle timeout of 0 means "no limit" (RFC 9000, 10.1) and no longer
    closes the connection on the next event loop pass.  See
    docs/SECURITY_AUDIT_PASS3_QUIC_2026-10-18.md and the pull request
    #6.

 -- Max <nahual15@gmail.com>  Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:05:00 +0000

ssh3-c (0.5.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 0.5.0: the pass-3 security audit of the QUIC
    stack (src/event/quic/*) and the closure of the review of its
    report.  The audit itself found no defect (the probes are clean:
    both presets 42/42, a 1 000 000-input ASan+UBSan fuzz run), the
    review did: the idle timeout of 0 means "no limit" (RFC 9000, 10.1)
    and not "fire now" - a server with -i 0 closed every connection
    before the handshake finished; the local address path of a wildcard
    listener was compiled out (the ancillary data check could never
    pass under the strict POSIX feature set, the setter decided
    nothing, and the kernel option was never set), so the replies of a
    multi-address host carried the routed source address; the odcid of
    a token is length-checked and copied instead of aliased into the
    packet buffer; the client id counter decrement is guarded.  See
    docs/SECURITY_AUDIT_PASS3_QUIC_2026-10-18.md.

 -- Max <nahual15@gmail.com>  Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:20:00 +0000

ssh3-c (0.4.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 0.4.1: the pass-2 security audit closure -
    the peer-advertised maxPacketSize rides the send path on both
    sides (P2-1), the constant-time compare for the exporter-derived
    bytes (P2-2), the jti replay cache of the verified tokens
    (P2-3), the login escapes into the JWT claims (P2-4), the
    reverse bind rewrite consumes a bounded local copy (P2-5), and
    the sftp -r (the recursive put|get) is reachable from the CLI
    again (P2-6).  See docs/SECURITY_AUDIT_PASS2_2026-10-18.md §10.

 -- Max <nahual15@gmail.com>  Sun, 18 Oct 2026 19:30:00 +0000

ssh3-c (0.4.0-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The openssh(8)-canon package split: the source now builds three
    binary packages - ssh3-client (the /usr/bin/ssh3 CLI with its
    fresh ssh3(1) man page), ssh3-server (the socket-activated
    daemon, Depends on the matching ssh3-client) and the ssh3c
    metapackage pulling the pair at matching versions (the `ssh'
    metapackage analog).
  * The drop-in conflict dance follows the split: ssh3-client
    Conflicts/Replaces ssh3-go-client, ssh3-server does the same
    against ssh3-go-server; the bundled deb/rpm/apk of build.sh
    declare the same against the split go packages.

 -- Max <nahual15@gmail.com>  Sun, 18 Oct 2026 19:00:00 +0000

ssh3-c (0.4.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 0.4.0: the client -o options and the -R of
    the product client, the server --gateway-ports and
    --max-reverse-forwards, the event-loop UAF and idle-close fixes,
    the fd-0 close fixes of the channel free path, the honest failure
    counting of the test mains, and the audit closures (F-1/I-1/I-2
    closed, I-3 verified).
  * The Debian packaging wave joins the release: this source package
    (quilt 3.0, debhelper 13, lintian-clean CI in the trixie
    container) ships beside the bundled build.sh deb/rpm/apk whose
    private OpenSSL 3.5 copy keeps the older distributions covered.
  * The binary package is a drop-in replacement for ssh3-go:
    Provides/Conflicts/Replaces against the same /usr/bin interfaces.

